        heading: "Electrical, Envelope, and the Old Cooler",
        body: "The electrical check is arithmetic the AHJ will verify. The engineer performs a load calculation on the existing service, adds the condenser, air handler, and any electric heat, and determines whether the panel and service conductors suffice or an upgrade is required. Many Albuquerque homes make the jump from 100 to 200 amps in the same project, which also future-proofs for an electric water heater or vehicle charger. The permit set shows the panel schedule, the feeder sizing, and the grounding - the details the electrical reviewer checks.\n\nThe old cooler leaves a hole, and the envelope repair is engineered, not patched. A roof curb removal gets the roof structure reframed, sheathed, dried-in, and flashed to match the existing roofing; a window unit opening gets reframed and finished to match the wall. The engineer specifies the repair so the thermal envelope and the weather barrier are continuous again - air sealing and insulation at the repair are part of the energy performance the conversion promises. Skipping this step carefully is how conversions develop the roof leaks owners blame on the new equipment.",
