        body: "New point loads need new footings. The engineer probes the existing foundation to confirm its width, depth, and condition, then designs pad footings under each new post - sized for the soil bearing capacity and detailed to avoid undermining the existing foundation during excavation. Where the ranch sits on expansive soils, the footing design accounts for movement so the new work does not crack away from the old. Underpinning is specified when the existing foundation itself is inadequate for the remodeled loads.\n\nPop-tops are evaluated as new structures on old foundations. The engineer checks whether the existing footings, foundation walls, and first-floor framing can carry the added story's gravity and lateral loads - often they cannot without reinforcement or a new independent foundation for the addition. The design coordinates the structural work with Denver's zoning limits on height and bulk plane, because a structurally feasible pop-top that violates zoning is a wasted design. Energy code compliance for the new envelope is integrated from the start rather than bolted on at permit time.",
